# Agent tool budget — parallel tools, citation order, turn cap, cache pricing

Status: not implemented. Written as a follow-up to raising `EVO_AGENT_MAX_STEPS`
from 4 to 12 and `EstimateChatMicros` from 6 to 48 credits. Those two numbers
cover the current serial loop; they do not make a 12-step turn cheap, and they
do not make the ledger honest.

## Summary

| ID | Severity | Issue | Fix size |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| H1 | High | A message's `tool_calls` run serially even though the loop already accepts several per step | Medium |
| H2 | High | `remember()` mutates `ctx.citations` inside each handler, so concurrent tools need ordered numbering | Small (once H1 exists) |
| M1 | Medium | No per-turn cumulative input-token budget; the step cap is the only brake | Medium |
| M2 | Medium | `credits_for_tokens` prices input flat; DeepSeek reports `prompt_cache_hit_tokens`, so long loops overcharge credits and overstate reconciled USD | Medium |
| L1 | Low | Prompt does not tell the model to batch tools into one message | Trivial |

Nothing below should land as a drive-by in an ingest/summary change.

